{
 "schema": "clean.crystal.markers_vacuity.v2",
 "date": "2026-08-19",
 "lane": "lane VAC",
 "what": "The marker-line ledger for clean-kernel at today's tip: the vacuity split of the `markers_exact` population, the shape of every refusal, and the RE-DERIVATION of the two figures docs/CRYSTAL_STATUS.md \u00a70.6 carried as ASSUMED \u2014 the marker residual of 13 and the 178 -> 192 marker ceiling. Supersedes the 2026-08-13 v1 record (data/crystal_markers_vacuity_2026-08-13.json), which stays as the historical measurement.",
 "instrument": {
  "built_here": "scripts/trust_ir_markers.py (new) \u2014 the per-row marker ledger and the residual derivation",
  "wired_into": "scripts/trust_ir_axes.py \u2014 7 new marker axes; `markers_lines_total`, `markers_differ_content` and `markers_unparseable` are GATED, the rest recorded",
  "reproduce": [
   "python3 scripts/trust_ir_markers.py ledger   --coverage <crate>.coverage.json",
   "python3 scripts/trust_ir_markers.py residual --o3 O3.coverage.json --o3-log O3.flip.txt --o0 O0.coverage.json --o0-log O0.flip.txt",
   "python3 scripts/trust_ir_markers.py selftest"
  ],
  "cost": "~2 s per whole-crate dump; no compiler"
 },
 "definition": {
  "vacuous": "markers_exact: true AND markers_detail == '0 marker line(s) identical' \u2014 two EMPTY marker sequences compared",
  "non_vacuous": "markers_exact: true AND markers_detail == 'N marker line(s) identical' with N > 0",
  "note": "Matching emptiness is honest agreement and is NOT a gate malfunction. This lane did not make empty sequences fail: that would refuse honest agreement and cost flips for nothing. The axis makes the split VISIBLE; it does not tighten the gate.",
  "built_vs_derived": "On the `markers differ` shape the sentinel `<end>` determines ONE side's length exactly and bounds the other. The producer (trust mir_differential.rs, frozen byte-identical for the crystal measurement) never writes both lengths, so `built_lines` / `derived_lines` are null where the artifact does not determine them \u2014 never 0. `0` is a measurement; `null` is its absence."
 },
 "headline": {
  "markers_exact": 1096,
  "vacuous": 1058,
  "non_vacuous": 38,
  "vacuous_fraction": "96.5%",
  "marker_lines_behind_the_whole_population": 129,
  "refused_rows": 463,
  "refused_rows_that_are_derived_side_EMPTY": 462,
  "refused_rows_that_are_a_CONTENT_disagreement": 0,
  "marker_lines_that_agreed_before_any_refusal": 0,
  "channel_skips": 1,
  "prior_record_2026_08_13": {
   "markers_exact": 1082,
   "vacuous": 1055,
   "non_vacuous": 27,
   "marker_lines": 105,
   "vacuous_fraction": "97.5%"
  }
 },
 "the_single_shape_of_every_refusal": "462 of 462 parseable refusals in clean-kernel diverge at LINE 0 with the DERIVED side `<end>`. Not one is a content disagreement, and not one carries a single agreeing marker line. So `markers_exact: false` in this crate does not mean 'the two marker sequences disagree'; it means 'the built side emitted storage markers and the MIR-derived side emitted none at all'. `level::Level::is_zero` is one of those 462, not a special case.",
 "what_markers_exact_true_is_worth": {
  "on_1058_of_1096_rows": "It certifies that NEITHER side emitted a storage marker in the walked blocks. That is a true statement about two empty sequences. It is not evidence: it has zero discriminating power against the failure the channel exists to catch, because the failure requires a marker to exist.",
  "on_38_of_1096_rows": "It certifies that the storage-slot liveness sequence \u2014 per-line block and statement position, slot index, and slot TYPE \u2014 is IDENTICAL between the THIR-built trust-ir and the MIR-derived trust-ir, over 129 marker lines in total, compared without normalization. That is a real, narrow structural fact about stack-slot lifetimes.",
  "what_it_never_certifies": "Semantic equivalence. The marker channel is a separate, normalization-free comparison layered on top of an already-`agreed` canonical verdict; its failure never downgrades the semantic verdict, and its success never upgrades one.",
  "the_sibling_axis_that_does_the_work": "Every markers_exact row also carries `N canonical line(s) identical` with N > 0 on 100% of them \u2014 3,645 canonical lines at this tip. The derived-MIR differential did real work on every row in the population. What it did not do on 1,058 of them is compare a MARKER sequence."
 },
 "re_derivation_of_the_two_assumed_numbers": {
  "method": "Both are read off one control lane's -O3/-O0 pair. At -O0 `RemoveStorageMarkers` makes a marker divergence codegen-immaterial, so the flip gate does not consult the marker verdict; the -O0-minus-(-O3) flip set is therefore what the marker gate costs. Joined by def_path ACROSS the two compiles (def_index is not stable across cfg-differing builds) and by def_index WITHIN one. Attribution is MEASURED, not assumed: each residual body is reported with its -O3 derived_mir verdict and marker class.",
  "control": "the marker CLASS census is BIT-IDENTICAL between the -O3 and -O0 arms (1058/38/462/1 in both), so the residual is a pure GATING difference, not a differential difference",
  "marker_residual_of_13": {
   "verdict": "REPRODUCES AS A NUMBER \u2014 BUT AS A DIFFERENT QUANTITY. Disagreement printed.",
   "measured_here": {
    "total_flip_event_residual": 13,
    "composition": {
     "differ-derived-empty": 12,
     "channel-skip": 1
    },
    "attributed_to_the_marker_gate": "13 of 13 (0 unattributed)",
