    "codegen_refused_subcount": 11,
    "codegen_channel_skip": 1,
    "ctfe_residual": 1
   },
   "what_section_4c_recorded_2026_08_13": {
    "codegen_residual": 14,
    "refused_subcount": 13,
    "channel_skip": 1,
    "ctfe_residual": "not reported"
   },
   "the_disagreement": "\u00a74c's 13 is the `refused` SUBCOUNT of a 14-event CODEGEN residual. Today's 13 is the TOTAL (codegen + CTFE) event residual, and the quantity \u00a74c called 13 now measures 11. The two 13s are not the same number wearing the same name. Anyone quoting 'the marker residual of 13' must now say which.",
   "continuity": "The single `marker channel(built)` skip is still `env::native_reducers_bool_ext::nat_gcd`, named identically on 2026-08-13 \u2014 the one row that survives both records unchanged."
  },
  "ceiling_178_to_192": {
   "verdict": "THE 192 ENDPOINT REPRODUCES EXACTLY; THE 178 ENDPOINT DOES NOT.",
   "measured_here": {
    "codegen_O3": 180,
    "codegen_O0": 192,
    "headroom_codegen": 12,
    "total_events_O3": 221,
    "total_events_O0": 234,
    "headroom_total": 13
   },
   "reading": "192 is confirmed on two independent drivers. 178 was the -O3 codegen count at an older tip; it is 180 today, which is what \u00a70.5/\u00a74h already record. The live ceiling is therefore 180 -> 192: TWELVE more codegen bodies would flip if the marker gate were satisfied, not fourteen. Stated as total flip events, 221 -> 234.",
   "what_the_ceiling_is_NOT": "An estimate of what marker work can win. Every one of the 13 residual bodies is refused because the DERIVED side emits no markers at all, so closing them is a derivation build item, not a comparison-tolerance question."
  }
 },
